experimental: strip optimization infrastructure and structural debt (#247)

## Summary

Second simplification pass. Remove caches, dead interfaces, and
duplication that survived the first pass (#245).

**Net: -1,522 lines (521 added, 2,043 removed) across 30 files**

## Removed

- `resourceCache` entirely (apply-hash skip for SSA Patch elision)
- Content-addressed compiled graph sharing and compilation key
computation
- `precompileExpressionChildGraphs` (design says child compiles
independently)
- `diffRevisionNodes` and revision-transition selective state
carry-forward
- Revision Ready/Active conditions (keep only GC)
- Dead metrics (`ResyncTimerFiresTotal`, `SelfRefreshTotal`)
- Dead watch interfaces (`DrainTriggers`, `DepositTrigger`,
`DrainCollectionChanges`, `CollectionChange`, `GetResourceVersion`,
`RetainWatches`)

## Simplified

- `graphCaches` flattened to `map[string]*instanceState`
- `compileRevision` reduced from 6 branches to 2
- `RouteEvent` simplified to identify-owner-and-enqueue
- Extracted `deletePreflight()` from duplicated prune/delete logic
- Decomposed `applySSA` into named steps (`prepareObject`,
`checkOwnership`, `ssaPatch`, `evictThirdPartyManagers`)
- Collapsed forEach carry-forward into single `forEachCarryForward`
struct
- `reconcileNode` returns `*nodeOutput` instead of `([]string,
*forEachState, error)` tuple

## Testing

- All E2E tests pass, 0 failures
- Unit tests pass with `-race`
- `go vet` clean
